  "goodToKnow": "Königlich means royal or regal: die königliche Familie, ein königliches Essen. Sich königlich amüsieren means to have a whale of a time. Germany has had no kings since 1918, when the monarchies of Bavaria, Prussia, Saxony and Württemberg ended, but many palaces carry königlich in their names. Note the ending -ig spoken like -ich in standard German: KÖ-nik-likh. Der König is king, and die Königin queen."
